        {
          "title": "Self-Knowledge Without Ownership",
          "body": "The memory source supplies a focused topic on the distinction between episodic ownership and other forms of self-knowledge. Trait self-knowledge, factual self-knowledge, voluntary scene recall, and some future planning can remain in place even when past scenes no longer feel personally owned."
        },
        {
          "title": "Decomposing Identity Vocabulary",
          "body": "This can be synthesized with the generalized-identity source because both distinguish different roles that may be conflated under one broad identity vocabulary. The metaphysical source separates generic essence, objectual essence, factual identity, and ground-theoretic status; the memory source separates event content, mineness, trait knowledge, and diachronic identity feeling."
        },
        {
          "title": "Structural Overlap Only",
          "body": "The conceptual overlap is structural rather than doctrinal. The page should not claim that generalized identity analyzes personal memory directly, but it can use the formal source as a contrast case for why identity claims often need decomposition into finer relations."
        }
